@startuml
title CCI Career Navigator — Save and Retrieve Matching Profile
caption Proposed flow only: persistence and API are not implemented

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #45645A
  LifeLineBorderColor #91A99E
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F5FAF7
  ParticipantBorderColor #52796F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #DCEFE5
  ParticipantFontColor #20352D
  ActorBorderColor #52796F
  ActorBackgroundColor #F5FAF7
  GroupBorderColor #98B4A7
  GroupBackgroundColor #F7FBF8
  NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E7
  NoteBorderColor #D6B86A
}

actor Student
participant "MatchingProfile.jsx\nIMPLEMENTED: React form and route-state navigation" as UI
participant "Express API\nPLANNED" as API
participant "Matching Profile Service\nPLANNED" as Service
participant "Prisma ORM\nSCAFFOLDED: client/schema only" as Prisma
database "PostgreSQL\nPLANNED: not connected" as DB

note over UI,DB
  This sequence describes the requested future user story, not current behavior.
  Today the questionnaire builds {careerInterest, skills, coursework,
  experienceLevel} and navigates to Recommendations using React Router state.
  There is no Express API, saved-profile Prisma model, profile migration,
  configured database, or authentication/ownership mechanism.
end note

Student -> UI: Complete career interest, skills,\ncoursework, and experience level
Student -> UI: Select "Find My Matches"
UI -> UI: Validate required selections and build matchingProfile
UI -> API: POST /api/matching-profiles\n{careerInterest, skills[], coursework[], experienceLevel}
activate API
API -> Service: Validate request and questionnaire values
activate Service

alt Invalid input
  Service --> API: Validation errors
  deactivate Service
  API --> UI: 400 Bad Request\n{errors}
  deactivate API
  UI --> Student: Show validation feedback
else Valid input
  Service -> Prisma: Create matching profile and related selections
  activate Prisma
  note right of Prisma
    Requires a new, team-approved Prisma model and migration.
    No such model exists in the approved schema.
  end note
  Prisma -> DB: INSERT matching profile and selections
  activate DB
  alt Database error
    DB --> Prisma: Error
    deactivate DB
    Prisma --> Service: Persistence error
    deactivate Prisma
    Service --> API: Save failed
    deactivate Service
    API --> UI: 500 Internal Server Error\n(generic client-safe response)
    deactivate API
    UI --> Student: Show save error; retain entered values
  else Save succeeds
    DB --> Prisma: Saved record and generated identifier
    deactivate DB
    Prisma --> Service: Saved profile
    deactivate Prisma
    Service --> API: Persisted profile
    deactivate Service
    API --> UI: 201 Created\n{matchingProfile}
    deactivate API
    UI --> Student: Display save confirmation

    ... Student returns later ...

    Student -> UI: Open Matching Profile
    UI -> API: GET /api/matching-profiles/{profileId}
    activate API
    API -> Service: Retrieve profile for authorized student
    activate Service
    Service -> Prisma: Find profile with selections
    activate Prisma
    Prisma -> DB: SELECT profile and related selections
    activate DB
    DB --> Prisma: Saved matching profile
    deactivate DB
    Prisma --> Service: Profile or not found
    deactivate Prisma
    Service --> API: Profile result
    deactivate Service
    API --> UI: 200 OK {matchingProfile}\n(or 404 Not Found)
    deactivate API
    UI --> Student: Restore saved selections\n(or prompt to create a profile)
  end
end

note over Student,DB
  Review before implementation: decide whether matching answers should persist,
  define student identity and ownership/authentication, approve the matching-
  profile schema and migration, and finalize endpoint and error contracts.
  Do not couple these answers to the separate localStorage Student Profile.
end note

@enduml
